WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:06.050
2018 is shaping up to be an intense year at
the cineplex, with numerous superhero movies,

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:08.860
Star Wars, and Harry Potter spin offs all
on the horizon.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:13.800
But for every film worth getting excited about,
there's another that we're absolutely dreading.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.010
From sequels and reboots that nobody asked
for to Biblical B-movies and poorly-timed

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:23.189
horrors, we're betting that the following
films will be the worst of the worst in 2018.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.189
Woody Woodpecker

00:00:24.189 --> 00:00:27.859
If you're a fan of the classic Woody Woodpecker
cartoons, then you'll definitely want to give

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:31.620
the upcoming live-action hybrid from Universal
a wide berth.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.100
"Guess who?"

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:41.500
This family-friendly adaptation of the screwball
'toon pits a CGI Woody Woodpecker against

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.730
a big-city lawyer who intends to tear down
his woodland home to create space for a new

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:46.730
development.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:50.530
Woody decides to takes matters into his own
hands and violently defends his home against

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:54.420
the construction crew, taking snaps on his
smartphone as he does.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.750
The trailer truly is the stuff of nightmares.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:00.230
The whole thing is clearly meant to be cheap
and cheery, but in the end it just comes off

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:05.960
as cheap, with the character so poorly rendered
in CG that his presence is completely jarring.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.759
Bizarrely, the film is already a hit in Brazil,
where an early release inexplicably grossed

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.860
more than $6.5 million.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:13.800
Go figure.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:15.640
"Here's Woody"

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:18.799
Samson

00:01:18.799 --> 00:01:23.020
The faith-based production company behind
the God's Not Dead trilogy are back with an

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:27.360
all-new biblical blockbuster this year, bringing
the tale of Samson to the big screen.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.399
Pure Flix has been making inroads in the Christian
market over the past few years, thanks largely

00:01:31.399 --> 00:01:35.359
to the success of their family-friendly home
streaming service, which offers gems like

00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:39.229
the Jeff-Foxworthy hosted The American Bible
Challenge.

00:01:39.229 --> 00:01:41.929
Chief executive Greg Gudorf told the New York
Times:

00:01:41.929 --> 00:01:44.520
"We've been blessed with really strong growth.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:48.810
Our God-given dream was to provide content
on a consistent basis to be an alternative

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:50.549
to what Hollywood was putting out."

00:01:50.549 --> 00:01:54.719
While the God's Not Dead films didn't require
much in the way of visual effects, Samson

00:01:54.719 --> 00:01:59.529
relies on them heavily, and the lack of funding
is highlighted by the substandard CGI.

00:01:59.529 --> 00:02:04.249
According to the Bible story, the Hebrew strongman
fought his way through 1,000 Philistines with

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:08.360
an animal bone and beat up a lion with his
bare hands, all of which is included in the

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:09.360
trailer.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:13.270
Sadly, the effects on show in these pivotal
moments seem pretty dated—the whole thing

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:16.860
looks like it was put together using deleted
scenes from The Mummy Returns.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:24.159
Add in some Billy Zane in a toy crown, and
you've got what looks to be a cinematic failure

00:02:24.159 --> 00:02:25.299
of Biblical proportions.

00:02:25.299 --> 00:02:29.430
"Never really understood what that meant until
right now."

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:31.670
Teen Titans Go! to the Movies

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:37.010
Cartoon Network's Teen Titans Go! has divided
DC fans since it started airing in 2013.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:40.819
Many viewers are of the opinion that the show
is an insult to both the original Teen Titans

00:02:40.819 --> 00:02:43.599
animated series and the much-loved comics
of the same name.

00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:48.200
Some have even petitioned the network to cancel
Teen Titans Go!, citing the bad messages it

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:52.120
sends to young viewers and the fact that it
more or less ignores the source material.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.299
"We blew it.

00:02:53.299 --> 00:02:57.239
All that goofing around and being silly ruined
this mission."

00:02:57.239 --> 00:03:01.459
Co-producer Michael Jelenic told Comics Alliance
that he's well aware of the "internet hate,"

00:03:01.459 --> 00:03:02.750
even though it's never slowed him down.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:07.420
He and his team have managed to thrash out
over 200 episodes in just four years, but

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.200
the move to the big screen will likely prove
to be a step too far.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:16.319
Teen Titans Go! to the Movies will follow
Robin, Starfire, Cyborg, Raven and Beast Boy

00:03:16.319 --> 00:03:20.480
to Hollywood as they go in search of a director
to make them famous with their very own superhero

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.840
movie—an idea that probably would have worked
better as a double episode rather than a full-length

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:26.069
feature film.

00:03:26.069 --> 00:03:29.650
Unfortunately, kids will probably clamor to
pay for an hour and a half of the same stuff

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:30.760
everybody hates about the show.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.840
"How you like that President Nixon?

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:34.380
Hah!

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:35.760
Back on the standard, baby!"

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:38.940
Slender Man

00:03:38.959 --> 00:03:43.980
In 2009, a Something Awful user posted a made-up
horror story and some doctored photos to the

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:48.290
website's forum, unaware of the chain of events
he'd set in motion.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:52.280
Before long, the faceless man he'd created,
with the ability to turn children against

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:57.400
one another, had become a genuinely popular
meme and, tragically, would go on to inspire

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.049
a real-life crime.

00:03:59.049 --> 00:04:03.209
Unsurprisingly, people have reacted angrily
to the news of a Slender Man movie.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.909
Even if it wasn't a totally insensitive move
by the studio, Sony still wouldn't be coming

00:04:06.909 --> 00:04:11.159
out of this well, because the trailer makes
the movie look downright awful.

00:04:11.159 --> 00:04:15.709
From creaking doors and jerking heads to creepy
forests and screaming schoolgirls, they break

00:04:15.709 --> 00:04:19.780
out every worn-out trope a horror fan could
think of, and then some.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:24.070
If you want to be scared this year, you're
better off looking just about anywhere else.

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:25.810
Alita: Battle Angel

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:30.340
Robert Rodriguez changed the way indie filmmakers
thought about GCI when he created the stunning

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:35.930
visuals in 2005's Sin City from his home studio,
faithfully adapting Frank Miller's beloved

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:37.280
graphic novels.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:42.400
The director has taken a similar approach
to the upcoming Alita: Battle Angel, his live-action

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.350
take on the manga Battle Angel Alita.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:50.410
The cyborg heroine is being played via motion-capture
by Rosa Salazar, whose eyes have been enlarged

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:53.250
to look as though they're straight out of
the pages of the comic.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.990
Talking about the bizarre concept, Robert
Rodriguez said:

00:04:55.990 --> 00:05:00.860
"The early artwork I saw that [James Cameron]
had, before it was even technically possible,

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:01.860
had that in her.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:05.889
It was so striking and so arresting, I thought,
'My god, we have to do that.

00:05:05.889 --> 00:05:09.770
We have to be the first to bring a true manga
and anime character to life.'"

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:12.471
"The eyes are the window to the soul.

00:05:12.471 --> 00:05:16.630
She's got some big windows to see, you know,
of the soul that goes on within that character,

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:19.630
cause the character has such great heart and
great soul."

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:22.951
While the filmmakers' intentions might have
been good, fans of the source material haven't

00:05:22.951 --> 00:05:25.750
been as positive about the design decisions.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:29.220
Considering the sordid history of live-action
manga adaptations, we're not holding onto

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.020
a lot of hope for this one.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:32.259
Peter Rabbit

00:05:32.259 --> 00:05:35.960
While it's now considered a classic of children's
literature, British author Beatrix Potter

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.650
actually had trouble getting The Tale of Peter
Rabbit published when she wrote and illustrated

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:41.850
it in the late 1800s.

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:45.949
In 1901, she decided to self-publish 250 copies
of the book with her own money.

00:05:45.949 --> 00:05:49.870
It went on to become a hit via word of mouth,
prompting one of the publishing houses who'd

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.590
previously turned her down to come crawling
back.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:55.669
In the years that followed, Potter turned
down plenty of offers to turn Peter Rabbit

00:05:55.669 --> 00:06:00.360
into a feature film, even rejecting offers
for an adaptation by Walt Disney himself.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.780
We'll never know what Disney's Peter Rabbit
might have looked like, but it's probably

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:08.120
safe to say that Potter would have hated the
brash party animal that Sony has turned him

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:09.120
into.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.950
Potter's relative, Nadine Hanwell, told The
Scottish Mail on Sunday:

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:14.120
"Beatrix Potter would be turning in her grave.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.669
I hope parents don't take their children to
see the film.

00:06:16.669 --> 00:06:18.979
She would absolutely loathe this."

00:06:18.979 --> 00:06:22.090
Reviews don't get much worse than that, but
it looks like there's a good reason for the

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.090
hate.

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:26.080
Peter was always mischievous in the books,
but in this interpretation, he's less cuddly

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.169
critter and more arrogant frat boy.

00:06:28.169 --> 00:06:29.900
"You must be Peter Rabbit.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:31.030
Yeah that's right."

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:35.190
Judging by the early reaction to the trailer,
this one is likely to be another major miss

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:36.400
for Sony.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.759
Hotel Transylvania 3: Summer Vacation

00:06:38.759 --> 00:06:43.000
Like the majority of Adam Sandler movies,
2012's Hotel Transylvania went down pretty

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:47.479
badly with the critics, only managing to score
44 percent on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:06:47.479 --> 00:06:51.040
Predictably, reviews for the 2014 sequel didn't
fare much better.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:55.570
After that flop, most people probably expected
the franchise to crawl back into its coffin.

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:59.080
"Why don't you just put a stake through my
heart."

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:03.129
So why are we staring down the barrel of a
third Hotel Transylvania movie?

00:07:03.129 --> 00:07:05.229
Basically, because they make a ton of money.

00:07:05.229 --> 00:07:10.129
The first two films were made for around $85
million each, yet they've pulled in staggering

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:16.199
amounts at the worldwide box office—$358
million and $473 million, respectively.

00:07:16.199 --> 00:07:20.449
A series of leaked emails in 2014 confirmed
that Sandler and the studio had fallen out

00:07:20.449 --> 00:07:25.020
over Hotel Transylvania 2, with the star apparently
wrestling control of the animated project

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:27.840
away from director Genndy Tartakovsky.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:32.629
Despite that giant mess, Sandler, Tartakovsky
and Sony all came back together to make a

00:07:32.629 --> 00:07:36.789
third Hotel Transylvania, putting financial
gain over professional pride.

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:41.580
We can probably expect Summer Vacation to
be the worst Hotel Transylvania yet.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:42.990
Fifty Shades Freed

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:46.729
Mocking the terrible dialogue littered throughout
the Fifty Shades of Grey novels was the internet's

00:07:46.729 --> 00:07:50.430
favorite game for a while, and it's hard to
argue against the haters when you actually

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:52.289
sit down to read the books.

00:07:52.289 --> 00:07:56.889
"He grabbed me suddenly and yanks me up against
him, one him at my back holding me to him,

00:07:56.889 --> 00:07:59.850
and another hand… oh my god, I'm not going
to say that."

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:01.069
To be fair to author E.L.

00:08:01.069 --> 00:08:05.449
James, she spotted a gap in the literary market
and plugged it, so to speak, cleverly tweaking

00:08:05.449 --> 00:08:08.740
what began as a bunch of Twilight fan fiction
for the mom audience.

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:12.949
A big-screen adaptation seemed inevitable
after the success of the raunchy trilogy,

00:08:12.949 --> 00:08:16.129
and there were more than a few fans who hoped
that the books' kinks would be ironed out

00:08:16.129 --> 00:08:17.129
in the process.

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:18.460
It hasn't happened.

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:19.740
"Seriously?"

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:20.340
"Yes."

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:27.099
Reviews for the first movie bashed almost
everything about it, and the second picture

00:08:27.099 --> 00:08:28.610
went down just as poorly.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:32.180
Judging by the trailer for the final installment,
Fifty Shades Freed, the filmmakers haven't

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:34.180
changed their approach one bit.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:38.000
Yeah, it'll probably rake in just as much
money as the first two installments in the

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:41.320
trilogy, but that doesn't mean it'll be a
pleasure to watch.

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:43.690
Viy 2: Journey to China

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:48.250
This adventure fantasy sequel pits action
stars Jackie Chan and Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:49.600
against one another.

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:50.780
In Russian.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.020
And Arnie is Captain Hook.

00:08:58.560 --> 00:08:59.460
Confused?

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:03.440
Well, to properly explain this wacky looking
Russo-Chinese production, we need to first

00:09:03.459 --> 00:09:07.779
mention that the previous movie, Viy: Forbidden
Empire, was the highest-grossing Russian film

00:09:07.779 --> 00:09:08.910
of 2014.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:12.790
The swashbuckling fantasy epic is based on
a classic horror novella first published in

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:17.920
1853, and the movie was even on track for
a U.S. release until a lawsuit between co-producers

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:18.920
derailed it.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:22.530
That may have been for the better, considering
that the few American critics that actually

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:24.790
got to see it weren't exactly blown away.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:28.810
But considering how much money the first film
made, a sequel was inevitable.

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:32.750
Only instead of concentrating on the positive
parts of the original, they seem to have embraced

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:33.750
the crazy.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:38.730
Chan and Schwarzenegger take top billing over
the original film's star, Jason Flemyng.

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:42.730
They both appear more than him in both trailers,
even though they're only supporting characters

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:44.500
in the continuation of his tale.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:48.900
The first film was guilty of favoring style
over substance, and that doesn't seem to have

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.320
changed for the sequel.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:51.320
Thanks for watching!

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:53.519
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:09:53.519 --> 00:09:55.649
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

